Article 2 (Selection of Persons Eligible for Early Promotion or Early Graduation)
When the head of an elementary school, middle school, high school or equivalent school (hereinafter referred to as "schools at each level") selects students eligible for early promotion or early graduation pursuant to Article 27 (1) of the Elementary and Secondary Education Act, the head shall comply with the standards prescribed by the superintendent of education concerning the following matters:
1. Academic achievement;
2. Scholastic aptitude, including results of intelligence tests;
3. Records of awards in domestic and international academic competitions and contests.
